Young's modulus,

\begin{aligned}
& Y=\frac{\text { stress }}{\text { strain }}=\frac{d F / A}{d l / x} \\
\Rightarrow \quad & d l=\frac{d F \cdot x}{A Y} \\
\Rightarrow \quad & d F=\frac{A Y d l}{x}
\end{aligned}

Where, $d F=$ centrifugal force due to mass of the element of length, $d x$.

\begin{aligned}
d F & =d m \cdot x \omega^2 \\
d F & =\frac{m}{L} \cdot x d x \omega^2 \\
& \quad \ldots \text { (ii) } \\
& {\left[\because \text { Change in mass } d m=\frac{m}{L} d x\right] }
\end{aligned}

From Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get

\begin{aligned}
\frac{A Y d l}{x} & =\frac{m}{L} \cdot x d x \omega^2 \\
\Rightarrow \quad d l & =\frac{m x^2 \omega^2}{L A Y} \cdot d x
\end{aligned}

⇒ Total change in length,

\begin{aligned}
l & =\int d l=\int_0^L \frac{m x^2 \omega^2}{L A Y} d x \\
& =\frac{m \omega^2 L^2}{3 A Y}=\frac{m}{A L} \cdot \frac{\omega^2 L^3}{3 Y}=\frac{\rho \omega^2 L^3}{3 Y}
\end{aligned}

